---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';

const path = '/for/subscription-boxes';
const title = 'Shopify cart recovery for subscription boxes';
const desc = 'Separate a new subscription, a gift and an existing subscriber’s account task.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
<a class="link" href="/for">Explore related guides</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Shopify cart recovery for subscription boxes</h1>
<p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Separate a new subscription, a gift and an existing subscriber’s account task.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Recover the commitment the shopper selected</h2>
<p>Store the selling plan, billing interval, first-box choice and destination alongside the product. A gift with a fixed term needs different wording from an automatically recurring plan. Show the introductory offer and subsequent charge clearly using the current checkout terms, including any shipping charged separately.</p>
<h2>Keep account servicing outside acquisition recovery</h2>
<p>A skip, renewal reminder, cancellation request or failed renewal payment is not evidence that someone abandoned a new subscription. Route account tasks to the subscriber portal or support owner. Before inviting someone to start again, check for an active plan and a recently completed order so the message does not create a duplicate subscription.</p>
<h2>Handle box rollover explicitly</h2>
<p>A saved checkout may refer to an earlier assortment. If the next box changes while a message is queued, show what can actually be ordered and ask the shopper to confirm it. Do not silently substitute a new theme or imply a guaranteed dispatch date after the cutoff. Coordinate stock reservations and gift delivery expectations with fulfillment.</p>
<h2>Evaluate first-box economics separately</h2>
<p>Calculate contribution from the initial shipment after product, packaging, delivery subsidy, acquisition incentive and channel cost. Future renewals are uncertain; show any assumed retention scenario separately from observed renewals. A discounted first box should not be called profitable because a spreadsheet assumes later billing.</p>
<h2>Proposed acceptance exercise</h2>
<p>Queue one gift and one recurring checkout. Roll the assortment forward, activate a plan through another session, and attempt to reopen both links. Inspect plan terms, gift wording, assortment, purchase exits and account routing. No test results are claimed here.</p>
<h2>Select by selling-plan evidence</h2>
<p>Require a finalist to show the actual selling-plan fields and active-subscriber exclusion, including what happens when subscription data arrives late. Compare <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">perishable delivery</a> and <a class="link" href="/for/supplements">supplement education</a>; recurring billing is shared, but box rollover and fixed-term gifting are the decisions here.</p>
</article>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
